WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.368
There are growing calls

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:04.471
inside Israel to halt controversial plans

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.072
for judicial reforms

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.040
after the sacking

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.641
of the defense minister

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.877
and massive protests on the streets.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.512
Thousands turned out in

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.747
Tel Aviv on Sunday

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:14.514
night after

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.482
Prime Minister Benjamin

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.751
Netanyahu fired Yoav Gallant

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.052
over his opposition

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.054
to a planned judicial overhaul.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.822
Reaction to that move

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:23.857
has been pouring in

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.192
with Israeli President Isaac Herzog

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.495
being the latest to speak out.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.063
In a post on Facebook,

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.132
he had this message for Netanyahu

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.533
saying, and I'm quoting,

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.801
The eyes of all

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.070
the people of Israel are on you.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.738
The eyes of all the Jewish

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.373
people are on you.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.376
The eyes of the whole world are on you

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.912
for the sake of the unity of Israelis,

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.515
for the sake of committed responsibility.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.682
I call on you

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.283
to halt

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.719
the legislative procedure immediately.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.755
And journalist Eliot Cohen was there

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.757
when the protests erupted on Sunday

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.426
and has more now from Tel Aviv.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.429
As the saying goes, if you're

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.229
going to shoot in the morning,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.164
you'd better not miss.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.131
And it seems that Israel's

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.700
now ex defense minister missed

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.169
when he gave a press conference

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.470
on Saturday evening

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.205
and became the first minister

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.573
to call for a halt

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.275
to this government's judicial overhaul,

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.042
because when

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.977
Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.113
returned for his weekend in London,

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.515
he sat galant and the result and that

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.150
is what you see behind me,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.985
thousands and thousands of people

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.221
on the streets of central Tel Aviv

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.489
showing their support

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.824
but galant in his opposition

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.325
to the overhaul

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.227
and reiterating their opposition

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.328
to an overhaul

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.896
that would remain pretty much all checks

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:37.530
and balances

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.131
on the government,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.999
allowing it to produce allies

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.468
in the Supreme Court

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.103
and preventing the Supreme Court

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.737
from striking down laws

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.306
passed by parliament,

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.842
except in very narrow circumstances.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:49.809
Says now

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.312
since its announcement by Netanyahu,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.446
since it came out

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.081
that he had sat in silence.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.082
These people have come out

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:56.683
onto the streets.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.717
They're usually out in the streets

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.885
for the past three months.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.621
On Saturday evenings and on Thursday.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.423
This is a Sunday evening.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.824
They are incredibly angry

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:05.859
that this has happened.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.360
We've heard from opposition

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.695
leaders like Yair Lapid

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.963
and from the prime minister

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.265
and Benny Gantz, former defense minister,

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:13.233
coming out and saying

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.202
that Netanyahu has crossed a red line.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.504
Former Prime Minister Ehud

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:19.305
Barak has sought for Netanyahu

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.306
to step down.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.374
The Histadrut, Israel's

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:21.941
main labor

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.244
union, has called for a general strike

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:25.245
on Monday.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.746
So if Netanyahu thought

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.014
that sacking Garland's

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.048
was going to quash

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.450
dissent in his ranks

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.152
and put an end to opposition

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.987
to this dismal overhaul,

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.788
he was very much mistaken.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:36.222
The scene

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.057
and this is any talk in Tel Aviv.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:40.760
Earlier, CNN spoke

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.228
with Yaakov Katz, editor

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.930
in chief at The Jerusalem Post

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.199
about the developments in Israel.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.567
And he weighed in on why

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.067
he thinks

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.202
Netanyahu decided

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:52.105
to sack his defense minister.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.940
I think what we saw last night

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.875
when he fired Yoav Galant,

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.210
the defense minister,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.179
was basically a decision

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:00.480
by Prime Minister Netanyahu.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.282
He is moving ahead with the legislation.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.950
They plan to bring it this morning

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.420
to finalize the piece of legislation

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.855
in the Knesset,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.089
the parliament's committee,

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.191
and finalize it

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.493
and prepared for a vote on Wednesday

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.562
when it will be brought for a second

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:16.329
and third reading.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.097
That's the final voting process

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.532
in the Israeli Knesset.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.134
And the reason to fire Galant,

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:21.668
I think, is

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.102
basically to send

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.637
a shot across the bow

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.972
and to create a deterrent

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:26.573
to tell

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.208
any other member of the coalition.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:31.377
If you dare cross me, if you dare violate

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.546
your commitment to my judicial reform,

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.714
I will fire you.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.216
And that is meant to get other people

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.817
who might be considering doing this

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.552
in the parliament to back off.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.821
Aaron David Miller is a

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.655
former Middle

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.456
East negotiator

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.390
for the State Department

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.191
and a senior fellow

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:46.593
at the Carnegie Endowment

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.560
He spent decades

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.195
working on American efforts

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.163
to broker agreements

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:52.198
between Israel and its neighbors.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.000
Good morning to you, Aaron.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.602
We appreciate you joining us.

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:56.736
Much of Israel

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.672
is at a standstill right now, the options

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:02.942
for Netanyahu at this hour.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.277
First of all, Daryn Kagan,

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.078
thanks for having me.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.279
Look, we're on terra

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.880
incognita, unprecedented.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.281
You now

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.549
have a general strike

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.950
which hasn't occurred,

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.784
I think it

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:12.151
since the

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.052
British mandate

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.955
for a period of of this size

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.925
we've been waiting for 3 hours for Mr.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.260
Netanyahu, the prime minister,

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.628
to make an appearance,

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:23.796
whose justice minister was out

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:24.998
earlier, basically

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:27.767
saying that he would accept any decision

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.901
that the prime minister made.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.403
And Mr.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.004
Levine,

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:31.904
the justice minister,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.373
is one of the hardest line

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:35.608
opponents of his judicial reform.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:38.177
I'd call it a judicial coup, actually.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:41.714
So I think Benjamin Netanyahu risk ready

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:42.815
on trial

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:43.916
for bribery, fraud,

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.151
breach of trust

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.819
wanted this judicial reform

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.321
to neuter the court.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.889
I think he may have no choice,

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.691
given the pressures that we've witnessed,

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.660
which are extraordinary.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.695
Basically, at least to push for building.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.597
Yeah, it's remarkable to hear

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:58.831
from the justice minister

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.199
coming out and saying that, given he

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.334
he was sort of the architect

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.335
of all of this.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:04.170
But one thing that I've been thinking

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.204
of in the bigger picture of

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:05.938
this is how much

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.340
does this have to do,

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.709
in your view, with Netanyahu himself?

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.144
Because you can't ignore that all of this

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:11.911
is coming

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:12.245
as he's

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.780
fighting his own corruption charges

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.181
and part of this new package,

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.983
the courts would no longer be able to bar

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.918
politicians who were convicted of crimes

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.087
from serving in top government jobs.

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:23.056
How much do you think this does have to

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:24.257
do with his own recent trial?

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.559
You know, Tip O'Neill

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.360
famously said

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.695
that all politics are local

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:30.430
when it comes to Benjamin Netanyahu,

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.731
particularly given the fact

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.800
that he's under indictment with a trial

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.401
in a Jerusalem district court

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.602
that's now three years

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:37.904
of continuing to run.

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.605
All politics are personal for him.

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.274
I think this is existential.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:42.375
And I think it explains

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:42.875
the risk

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.377
readiness, the abandonment

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:45.945
of caution and prudence

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.013
that have characterized

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:49.549
so much of Benjamin Netanyahu's career.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:50.650
One step forward,

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.486
one step back, back where he really needs

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.388
his judicial reform.

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:58.391
I think he now has, as we understand,

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.393
that he's not going to get it.

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.762
I think five elections,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.364
the Israelis have had in

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:06.366
almost four years, driven

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.433
by the fact that Mr.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.769
Netanyahu not agree to the formation

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:10.937
of any government

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:11.504
in which he did

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.573
not have a majority in large part

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:15.541
because of his trial.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.075
Yeah.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.777
Listen, it's not just Gilad there.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:19.879
At least two more Israeli ministers,

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.081
both of the same party as Netanyahu,

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:22.782
they suggested

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:25.418
halting this controversial plan as well.

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:25.952
The former

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.954
prime minister, Yair Lapid,

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:30.356
called Gallant's dismissal a new low.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.492
And I think what he's saying is

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:33.793
what's happening now, he's

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:34.460
he wrote on Twitter

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.161
that Netanyahu

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.796
may be able to fire the minister,

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.331
but he cannot fire the people of Israel

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:39.932
who are standing up to the insanity

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:40.967
of the coalition.

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.034
That appears to be true.

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.705
You know, that is such a crucial point.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:46.239
And, you know,

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:47.707
what's the takeaway for us?

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:48.141
Israel

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:49.442
and the US are fundamentally

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:50.176
different countries,

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:50.643
and it's hard

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.578
to compare our circumstances

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.414
but the reality is

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.348
indictments,

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:57.450
impeachments, investigations,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.584
all of that

00:06:58.584 --> 00:06:59.752
notwithstanding

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:00.553
what is happening

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.321
in the streets of Israel struggling

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:02.822
for what

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:03.923
many Israelis believe is

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:06.092
the soul of their country,

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.361
is people power.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:09.862
And it's extraordinary.

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:10.163
It may

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:12.565
well it may well be one of the takeaways

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:13.900
despite the differences

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.635
that divide the US and Israel,

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.636
the type of system

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:17.503
we have,

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.839
largeness and smallness of this country.

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.942
One take away that maybe Americans

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.310
ought to consider.

00:07:24.544 --> 00:07:25.311
What are you?

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:25.778
Aaron,

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:26.946
what do you think is going to happen?

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.347
I know you don't like to predict things.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:28.915
Do you think he's going

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:29.649
to have to back down

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.050
or at least freeze it for a moment?

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.052
I don't you

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:33.586
know, Don, and

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:34.320
I think

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.621
the Oracle of Delphi

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:36.355
probably couldn't

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:37.390
make a prediction right now.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.425
But I think if I had to predict,

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.860
it just seems to me

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:41.828
to be straining

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.062
the bounds of credulity

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:44.597
to the breaking point

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:45.731
that he won't push

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:47.433
for some sort of delay.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.802
The country is in the verge of a crisis.

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.471
And while they haven't been violence,

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:53.406
that's always a real possibility

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:55.141
the longer that this could happen.

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:55.775
Yeah.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.710
Aaron David Miller, thank you for that.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:58.478
I mean, just the fact

00:07:58.478 --> 00:08:00.446
that the justice minister is saying

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:01.814
that he'll accept whatever

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.716
Netanyahu decides could be an indication

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:05.418
that he may he may back off

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:07.153
even if it temporarily delays it.

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:08.421
We'll see. We'll be watching.

